hi and welcome to another gamespot  unboxing this time we have the brand new  xbox series x  now you might have seen that we've done  a bunch of tech tests on it already  but this is a final retail unit so i'm  going to be opening it  up and having a look at what's inside  let's take a quick look at the packaging  pretty standard fare kind of awkward  that it's still got halo on the back  but delays happen obviously all the info  about what is actually  inside the box all right razer blade  time let's  open this up  okay  it's literally gift wrapped like a  present  which is nice hopefully people be  getting these for christmas i suppose  let's look at the accessories first  standard  product and regulatory guide warranty  stuff  not very exciting at all okay we have  an hdmi 2.1 cable and we know it's a 2.1  because it says  ultra high speed on it that is the uh  the designation given  to 2.1 hdmis so if you want to be  playing games  upwards of 4k you need one of these bad  boys  here you've got the power cable probably  saw this go viral on twitter a few  while ago uh it is just a standard ac  power cable  if you're using a power cable for your  xbox one x for example  that should actually work with your  series x we had michael heim test that  out  a couple weeks ago okay new controller  so comes with batteries very useful  although along for the day when they'll  finally just have a rechargeable one and  don't need  double a batteries this is the brand new  controller this is my first  hands-on with it i use the xbox elite  series 2  a lot i've been using the dual sense as  well a lot so i can compare it to that  as well as a dualshock 4  and a standard xbox one controller but  first impressions  is that it feels very light they have  these kind of like the texturized  uh plastic on the grips and now on the  triggers which just i mean like it's  still a great controller  a little too light for my taste i like  the fact that the elite is much heavier  i mean face buttons just feel like an  xbox controller  they have redesigned the d-pad but yeah  it feels nice feels more in line with  how i like it on the elite  uh brand new button uh you have a share  a designated share button now so no  longer  is the view button a weird kind of  mashup of a button  now you have a dedicated share button  which is useful for sharing screenshots  and gameplay but other than that it's  like a standard standard xbox controller  it feels nice in the hand but i still  prefer my elite  uh but obviously with the xbox ecosystem  the xbox family  uh all the accessories you had for your  xbox one will work with the new  xbox series s and x and speaking of x  let's open the console time to power my  dreams  good lord it's heavy  that was a legitimate reaction i wasn't  expecting it to be that heavy  merry christmas xbox please put that  clip of usher in  merry christmas xbox it's usher and i  hope that santa got you everything you  asked for including  dan central 3. i'll see you guys in the  new year clearly in quarantine  i haven't been doing any weights um this  is quite heavy  it feels very dense you know it feels  like there's definitely a lot in there  let's go through everything power button  oh that's quite a hard button to press  i don't know if that makes a difference  but if you remember when the original  xbox one came  out the button that was not even really  a button that would turn on  if there was like a waft of air in in  its general direction so it feels  actually quite good to have something  that's quite tactile and gives you  feedback  the disk drive so if you get an xbox  series x  it comes with a disk drive which is very  useful if you buy a lot of games on disk  if you don't then maybe the xbox series  s  is the better option for you but this  drive here and eject  uh disk button button to sync your  controller and a usb  a port we'll move to this side because  this is the side that will be  lying on your desk or table or whatever  it is  you want to put your series x if you  want to have it horizontally so you've  got these like rubberized grips here i  assume that the same ones that are on  the bottom  provide a lot of grip it's actually  quite difficult to move it okay move  around the back of the console now  two more usb uh ports same as the one on  the front of the console  here's where you're gonna put your  ethernet cable if you wanna have it  wired into the internet  here's where your power adapter is gonna  go here is your hdmi out and like i said  it comes with an hdmi 2.1 cable  and also here you have the storage  expansion slot  so storage expansion on the series x  works slightly differently  you can buy an official storage  expansion card which currently runs at  about 220  which is obviously quite a lot of money  for extra storage if you're going to be  downloading loads and loads of games  you don't think that the one terabyte  internal storage is going to be enough  there are options for you there are the  official storage  uh card like i mentioned but if you want  to go on gamesup.com michael has done a  rundown of  testing external hard drives just usb  hard drives and kind of weighing up the  load times  of games that are on external hard  drives compared to using the internal  storage  so go check that out if that's going to  be a big issue or a big selling point  for you  and then on this side just plain  plain side it's got my grubby  fingerprints all over it now let's take  a look  at the bottom so the bottom is actually  just all one of these  big rubberized grips no wonder she  wasn't moving when i was trying to pick  her up and move her about  but let's look at the top oh god  and so the top is where you'll get that  splash of color that xbox green  uh in the vents in the top here i  remember the first time at the game  awards when we got that look  uh the first ever look at the series x  and everyone was just talking about  how monolithic it seemed and how huge  and honestly  considering the power that you've got  inside this thing this is smaller than  it should be  honestly like now seeing it in the flesh  i can totally see where it's gonna live  in my house  you know it just it just seems to fit in  i'm actually kind of surprised at how  small it is  this is a decently sized console and  then the final thing in the box  uh you've got a little getting started  quick start guide  which could also double as something to  hang on your door if you don't want to  be disturbed because you're gaming too  hard  that's a joke it doesn't actually say  that just tells you to go download the  xbox app and use quickstart to get it  all set up and running  so that was the unboxing of the xbox  series x  obviously for more on the brand new  console as well as the series s  and playstation 5 keep your eyes peeled  to gamespot  [Music]  you

